{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"☀️ §8 — Nothing Happens Without a Controller\n\nThis chapter taught two objects that have nothing to do with each other.\n\nOne routes HTTP by hostname and path at the edge of the cluster, at layer 7, for traffic co"}},"session_id":"7de0e91d-683b-4a51-921f-11310e8a0bec","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"4fe122d1-c677-4e0b-9e53-8e52171f7836"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ming in from outside. The other permits and forbids TCP connections between Pods inside it, at layers 3 and 4, for traffic that never leaves. Different layers. Different directions. Different problems. In most organisations, different teams.\n\nAnd they fail the same way.\n\nWrite"}},"session_id":"7de0e91d-683b-4a51-921f-11310e8a0bec","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"8acf974a-84ac-4b3f-b712-1857843fa496"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" either one perfectly. Apply it successfully. Watch `kubectl get` return it. And nothing happens, because in one case no Ingress controller is installed, and in the other the network plugin does not implement NetworkPolicy.\n\n> ☀️ **Zenith:"}},"session_id":"7de0e91d-683b-4a51-921f-11310e8a0bec","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"5e665265-fd61-450c-8cb7-a30a8198b892"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"**\n>\n> You have now seen this four times, and two of the four were your own from last chapter.\n>\n> A `type: LoadBalancer` Service with no provider to fulfil it. A Service whose selector matched no Pods. An Ingress with no controller. A NetworkPolicy"}},"session_id":"7de0e91d-683b-4a51-921f-11310e8a0bec","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"0523ebad-459e-4817-ae89-3f5e753f2dcd"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" on a plugin that does not implement one.\n>\n> Chapter 3 gave you the sentence — *an object without its component does nothing* — and told you that you would meet it four more times. This is where that debt comes due in full.\n>\n> But"}},"session_id":"7de0e91d-683b-4a51-921f-11310e8a0bec","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"dfb5a7c4-ebf7-4164-97ee-1fd41becf609"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" the rule is not a fact about Ingress, and it is not a fact about NetworkPolicy. It is a fact about **what a Kubernetes object is**, which you have held since Chapter 4 without necessarily seeing where"}},"session_id":"7de0e91d-683b-4a51-921f-11310e8a0bec","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"a6b5c885-79d2-4f36-b26e-2d0051fe13f9"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" it led.\n>\n> An object is a record of intent. Intent does not act.\n>\n> Something has to be watching, and willing, and *present*. Every object in this book works this way: the Deployment that produced"}},"session_id":"7de0e91d-683b-4a51-921f-11310e8a0bec","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"78617cd4-d742-49be-bfa3-e52c8cb639ef"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":" Pods, the Service that produced a stable name, the Job that ran to completion. In all of those cases the watcher happened to be there, so the object appeared to do the work itself. These four are simply the cases where the watcher is missing, and the appearance falls away.\n\nA chart drawn perf"}},"session_id":"7de0e91d-683b-4a51-921f-11310e8a0bec","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"49c4f485-5276-4cbe-afaa-eb3c04058c8a"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"ectly is still a chart. Somebody has to stand the watch.\n\nYou did not need the book to tell you this, incidentally. Soundings question 6 asked you to write down Chapter 3's rule and name a place you had met it, and if you answered that question you had already"}},"session_id":"7de0e91d-683b-4a51-921f-11310e8a0bec","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"173a4db0-c50e-4c9d-b05b-6d63cc4198a6"}
